## Why This Is Asked
CKNE-aware storage demonstrates practical cost-latency optimization at scale. This evaluates the candidate's ability to design tiering policies, maintain SLA guarantees, and implement preemption with telemetry.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE score mapping to storage tiers and TTL policies
- Per-tenant fairness mechanisms and preemption rules
- Minute-level control loop with capacity rebinding
- Comprehensive telemetry for performance monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo implementation
setInterval(() => {
  tenants.forEach(tenant => {
    if (tenant.ckne < 0.3) {
      migrateToLowerTier(tenant);
      rebindCapacity(tenant, false);
    } else if (tenant.ckne > 0.7) {
      prioritizeCapacity(tenant);
    }
  });
}, 60000);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-hop, CKNE-aware backpressure and fairness across thousands of tenants with SLA-based tuning.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health as a control signal for fan-out
- Per-tenant token bucket and dynamic scaling
- SLA-tier influences on limits and queuing
- Edge backpressure signaling and aggregation
- Payload schemas and end-to-end test plan

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeLimit(health, queueLen, sla) {
  const base = 1000;
  if (health > 0.8 && queueLen < sla.maxQueue * 0.7) return Math.min(base * 5, sla.maxCap);
  if (health < 0.4 || queueLen > sla.maxQueue * 0.9) return Math.max(base * 0.2, sla.minCap);
  return base;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
